# What this patches: apps/remix/app/components/general/app-nav-desktop.tsx and
#   app-nav-mobile.tsx — the two definitions of the team-level main nav. Adds a
#   "Leases" entry beside Documents and Templates, rendered only for teams whose
#   organisation holds the `lease-builder` feature.
#
# Why not a new file: the nav items are array literals inside these two
#   components. There is no shared, importable definition to extend — upstream
#   extracted the SETTINGS nav to packages/lib/utils/settings-nav.ts in the
#   2026-08-13 sync (see overlays/README.md "Relocations") but did not do the
#   same for the app nav, and each component still builds its own array with its
#   own item shape (`label` + `msg` on desktop, `text` + `t` on mobile). A new
#   file cannot add an entry to a literal it cannot see.
#
# Upstream-merge-fragility: LOW.
#
# Both insertions are a single spread expression appended to an array that
# upstream already maintains as data, plus an import and a hook call. That is
# the shape overlay 047 had to CREATE for the admin sidebar; here upstream has
# already done it, so this overlay only adds a row. A merge conflict is possible
# if upstream reorders or restyles the array, and the fix in that case is to
# re-append the same one line — there is no logic to re-derive.
#
# The gate is the interesting part. `canAccessLeaseBuilder` is server-only and
# these components render in the browser, so the flag reaches them through a
# READ of the gate rather than a copy of it: `bizrethink.leaseBuilder.access`
# (additive, packages/bizrethink) calls the same function every lease route's
# loader calls, and apps/remix/app/components/general/lease/
# use-lease-builder-team-urls.tsx maps its answer onto the session's team tree.
# Nothing about the rule lives in an upstream file, so a future upstream sync
# cannot silently change who sees the entry. Guarded by
# packages/bizrethink/regression-tests/leases-nav-entry.test.ts, which fails if
# the entry is dropped from either file or stops being gated on that hook.
#
# Alternatives considered and rejected: putting the flag on the organisation
# session (would patch upstream's session query AND its zod schema, and add two
# grant lookups per organisation to a query that re-runs on every navigation and
# window focus), and threading a boolean through a route loader (the nav is
# rendered by _authenticated+/_layout.tsx, which sets
# `shouldRevalidate = () => false` — its loader does not re-run on a team
# switch, so the boolean would describe whichever team was landed on first).

